+# Airflow 3.3 Deployment Checklist
+
+## Pre-Deployment
+
+- [ ] Review this checklist and MIGRATION_NOTES.md
+- [ ] Ensure platform team has tested Airflow 3.3.2 in staging
+- [ ] Notify growth team of Monday evening maintenance window
+
+## Deployment Steps
+
+### 1. Update Airflow Version
+```bash
+# Install from requirements.txt
+pip install -r requirements.txt
+
+# Verify
+python -c "import airflow; print(airflow.__version__)"
+# Expected: 3.3.2
+```
+
+### 2. Deploy Updated DAG Files
+```bash
+# Copy to Airflow DAG directory
+cp dags/weekly_campaign_report.py /path/to/airflow/dags/
+cp dags/campaign_sync.py /path/to/airflow/dags/
+
+# Verify DAGs load in Airflow UI
+airflow dags list | grep -E "weekly_campaign_report|campaign_sync"
+```
+
+### 3. Validate DAGs in Airflow
+```bash
+# Test DAG parsing
+airflow dags test weekly_campaign_report $(date -d "Monday" +%Y-%m-%d)
+
+# Verify schedule was parsed correctly
+airflow dags show weekly_campaign_report | grep schedule
+# Expected: 0 6 * * 1
+```
+
+## Post-Deployment (Day 1)
+
+### 4. Configure Deadline Alerts (In Airflow UI)
+
+**For `weekly_campaign_report` DAG:**
+
+1. Navigate to Admin → Deadline Alerts (or DAG → Deadline Alerts in newer versions)
+2. Click "Create Deadline Alert"
+3. Configure:
+   - **DAG ID:** `weekly_campaign_report`
+   - **Timeout:** 3 hours (from DAG start)
+   - **Callback Function:** `notify_growth_deadline_alert`
+   - **Description:** "Growth dashboard SLA: Monday report must complete by 09:00 UTC"
+4. Click "Save"
+
+### 5. Verify Monday Report Works
+- [ ] Monday 06:00 UTC: weekly_campaign_report starts
+- [ ] Check logs: Should have `summarize_week` → `publish_manifest`
+- [ ] Verify output files created:
+  - `output/weekly/<YYYY-MM-DD>.csv`
+  - `output/manifests/<YYYY-MM-DD>.json`
+- [ ] Confirm growth team can access dashboard
+
+### 6. Verify Hourly Sync Works
+- [ ] Confirm campaign_sync runs hourly
+- [ ] Check `output/reference/campaigns.csv` is updated
+- [ ] No error logs for catchup (catchup=False prevents backfill)
+
+## Rollback Plan (If Issues)
+
+If the Airflow 3.3 deployment has critical issues:
+
+1. **Stop Airflow scheduler/webserver**
+2. **Revert to 2.11.2:**
+   ```bash
+   pip install apache-airflow==2.11.2
+   ```
+3. **Restore old DAG files from git:**
+   ```bash
+   git checkout 534efeb -- dags/
+   ```
+4. **Restart Airflow**
+5. **Report incident** to platform team
+
+## Known Differences from 2.11
+
+| Feature | Airflow 2.11 | Airflow 3.3 | Notes |
+|---------|-------------|------------|-------|
+| DAG Definition | @dag decorator | with DAG context | Task logic unchanged |
+| Schedule Parameter | schedule_interval | schedule | Cron expressions work the same |
+| SLA Handling | default_args sla | Deadline Alerts | Configure post-deployment |
+| Import Path | airflow.decorators | airflow.sdk.definitions | SDK is new standard |
+| Python Version | 3.8+ | 3.9+ | Verify your Python version |
+
+## Troubleshooting
+
+### DAGs not appearing in UI
+- Check DAG files are in correct directory
+- Run `airflow dags refresh`
+- Check logs: `airflow dags list`
+
+### Tasks failing with import errors
+- Verify `airflow.sdk.definitions` is importable: `python -c "from airflow.sdk.definitions.dag import DAG"`
+- Check Python version: `python --version` (should be 3.9+)
+
+### Schedule not running at expected time
+- Verify cron expression: `0 6 * * 1` = Monday 06:00 UTC
+- Check timezone settings in Airflow config (should use UTC)
+- Verify scheduler process is running: `airflow scheduler`
+
+### "SLA feature is deprecated" warnings
+- This is expected; SLA is deprecated in 3.3+
+- Deadline Alerts configuration will suppress these warnings
+- No action needed if alerts are configured
+
+## Support
+
+For questions or issues:
+1. Check MIGRATION_NOTES.md for detailed changes
+2. Review Airflow 3.3 release notes: https://airflow.apache.org/docs/apache-airflow/3.3.0/release_notes.html
+3. Contact platform team for deployment issues
+
+## Sign-Off
+
+- [ ] Growth team lead: Verified Monday report requirements
+- [ ] Platform team lead: Airflow 3.3 deployment complete
+- [ ] Data team: Confirmed DAG functionality
+
