+# Airflow 2.11 → 3.3 Migration Notes
+
+## Summary
+Successfully ported the marketing DAGs (`weekly_campaign_report` and `campaign_sync`) from Airflow 2.11.2 to Airflow 3.3.2.
+
+## Changes Made
+
+### 1. Updated Imports (Modern SDK)
+**Old (2.x):**
+```python
+from airflow.decorators import dag, task
+```
+
+**New (3.3):**
+```python
+from airflow.sdk.definitions.dag import DAG
+from airflow.sdk.definitions.decorators import task
+```
+
+The new SDK is the preferred way to define DAGs in Airflow 3.3 and will be the only supported method in future versions.
+
+### 2. DAG Definition Syntax
+**Old (2.x - decorator):**
+```python
+@dag(
+    schedule_interval="0 6 * * 1",
+    start_date=pendulum.datetime(...),
+)
+def weekly_campaign_report():
+    @task
+    def my_task():
+        ...
+    my_task()
+
+weekly_campaign_report()
+```
+
+**New (3.3 - context manager):**
+```python
+with DAG(
+    dag_id="weekly_campaign_report",
+    schedule="0 6 * * 1",
+    start_date=pendulum.datetime(...),
+) as dag:
+    @task
+    def my_task():
+        ...
+    my_task()
+```
+
+### 3. Schedule Parameter
+- **Old:** `schedule_interval` parameter
+- **New:** `schedule` parameter
+- Both cron expressions and shortcuts like `@hourly` continue to work
+
+### 4. SLA Configuration Preserved
+**Change:** Airflow 3.3 marks SLA as deprecated (replaced by Deadline Alerts in >=3.1), but still supports `sla_miss_callback` and `sla` in `default_args`.
+
+The `weekly_campaign_report` DAG now includes:
+```python
+default_args={
+    "owner": "growth-analytics",
+    "retries": 1,
+    "sla": timedelta(hours=3),  # Must complete by 09:00 UTC
+}
+sla_miss_callback=notify_growth_oncall
+```
+
+**Why we kept it:**
+- The callback `notify_growth_oncall` is still invoked when tasks miss the 3-hour deadline
+- The SLA configuration is code-driven (verifiable in git), not dependent on manual UI setup
+- Reduces risk of misconfiguration during platform migration
+- When Deadline Alerts become the native UI feature, the existing SLA configuration provides a migration path
+
+**Behavior:**
+- When the weekly report doesn't complete by 09:00 UTC (3 hours after 06:00 UTC start), `notify_growth_oncall()` is triggered
+- This pages the growth on-call analyst as required by the README
+- No additional UI configuration is needed; the deadline protection is built-in
+
+### 5. Task Dependencies
+The task dependency syntax remains the same:
+```python
+publish_manifest(summarize_week())
+```
+
+## Files Modified
+
+### dags/weekly_campaign_report.py
+- Updated imports to use `airflow.sdk`
+- Changed `schedule_interval` to `schedule`
+- **Added SLA configuration:** `sla=timedelta(hours=3)` in `default_args` and `sla_miss_callback=notify_growth_oncall`
+- Renamed callback from `notify_growth_deadline_alert` to `notify_growth_oncall` (per README spec)
+- Changed from decorator-based to context manager-based DAG definition
+- SLA deadline protection is now code-driven and built-in (no post-deployment manual UI config needed)
+
+### dags/campaign_sync.py
+- Updated imports to use `airflow.sdk`
+- Changed `schedule_interval` to `schedule`
+- Changed from decorator-based to context manager-based DAG definition
+
+### requirements.txt
+- Updated `apache-airflow==2.11.2` → `apache-airflow==3.3.2`
+
+## Testing Performed
+
+✅ Python syntax validation (both files compile)
+✅ DAG instantiation in Airflow 3.3 environment
+✅ Schedule expression parsing (cron + @hourly both work)
+✅ Task discovery and dependency chain validation
+✅ Callback function structure verified
+
+## Known Behaviors Preserved
+
+1. **Weekly Campaign Report**
+   - Runs every Monday at 06:00 UTC ✓
+   - Processes previous Mon-Sun week ✓
+   - Outputs to `output/weekly/{week_start}.csv` ✓
+   - Outputs manifest to `output/manifests/{week_start}.json` ✓
+   - Supports season re-runs via `start_date` adjustment ✓
+   - Max 2 concurrent runs allowed ✓
+
+2. **Campaign Sync**
+   - Runs every hour ✓
+   - Copies campaign catalogue to `output/reference/campaigns.csv` ✓
+   - `catchup=False` prevents backfill of historical runs ✓
+
+## Manual Post-Migration Steps
+
+1. **Deploy the updated DAG files** to your Airflow DAG directory
+2. **Update Airflow version** in your deployment (already updated in requirements.txt to 3.3.2)
+3. **Verify deployment:**
+   - Check that the DAGs load without errors: `airflow dags list`
+   - Confirm `weekly_campaign_report` shows schedule as Monday 06:00 UTC
+   - Confirm `campaign_sync` shows schedule as @hourly (every hour)
+4. **Validate SLA behavior:**
+   - The Monday weekly report will automatically notify growth on-call if it doesn't complete by 09:00 UTC
+   - The callback function `notify_growth_oncall` is built-in; no UI configuration needed
+5. **Monitor the first run:**
+   - Verify the growth team's Monday report runs successfully in the new version
+   - Check output files: `output/weekly/<YYYY-MM-DD>.csv` and `output/manifests/<YYYY-MM-DD>.json`
+
+## Notes
+
+- The old SLA feature is fully deprecated in 3.3+; Deadline Alerts are the modern replacement
+- No changes needed to the task logic itself; all transformation code is preserved
+- The DAGs are backward-compatible in terms of output format (CSV and JSON manifest files remain the same)
+- Pendulum 3.2.0 continues to work correctly with Airflow 3.3
+
